# G-PLAN exact-phrase allowlist: `path-part|exact phrase`. A phrase is cut from a hit only when the file path contains the
# path AND the line contains the phrase. Keep each entry to one legit use; never allow a whole word or a price.
# "Google Cloud" is the provider's own name in the Google API key rule text (checks/secrets.ts); shown to the user as-is.
packages/cli/src/checks/secrets.ts|access Google Cloud services or Google Maps
packages/cli/src/checks/secrets.ts|Restrict key usage in the Google Cloud Console
# Comment in core/verdict.ts about the headline; the file belongs to W2a, which can reword it and delete this line.
packages/cli/src/core/verdict.ts|release gate can produce
# Rule texts in the shipped free bundle (generated from the rule corpus) that name cloud providers or cloud accounts
# in the generic sense, plus one provider documentation URL. Not product claims. Exact phrases only.
rules/free-bundle.json|https://cloud.google.com/iam/docs/best-practices-for-managing-service-account-keys
rules/free-bundle.json|API keys, database URLs, signing keys, cloud credentials
rules/free-bundle.json|enables full cloud account takeover
# The same rule texts as they appear in the built CLI (dist/ of the pack; chunk names change per build, so the path part is dist/).
dist/|access Google Cloud services or Google Maps
dist/|Restrict key usage in the Google Cloud Console
dist/|https://cloud.google.com/iam/docs/best-practices-for-managing-service-account-keys
dist/|API keys, database URLs, signing keys, cloud credentials
dist/|enables full cloud account takeover
